              "text": "मोची (mochī) goes back to Sanskrit mocika, \"tanner and cobbler\", recorded in Buddhist Sanskrit and built on moca, \"shoe\" (CDIAL 10349). CDIAL takes moca from an Iranian source, comparing Pahlavi (Middle Persian) mōč, \"shoe\"."
